<title>UK: Costa Rica becomes 47th member of ISO.</title>
<headline>Costa Rica becomes 47th member of ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Costa Rica has joined the International Sugar Agreement 1992, becoming the 47th member of the London-based International Sugar Organization (ISO), the ISO said in a statement on Wednesday. It joined the Agreement on October 11, the statement said. In 1995 Costa Rica produced 355,000 tonnes of sugar, raw value, exported 146,000 tonnes and consumed 195,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>With the addition of Costa Rica, the ISO's member countries represented 66.1 percent of world sugar output and 46.2 percent of consumption, based on data for 1995, the statement said.</p>
<p>They accounted for 87.7 percent of world sugar exports and 18.8 percent of imports, it added.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
